# Western Blotting


@left


- In western blotting or immunoblotting, proteins are separated in an SDS-PAGE gel, transferred to a polymer, and then stained with a fluorescent antibody.


@right


![Instructor figure related to protein gels and western blotting](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_020.jpg)

- Quick check: What does an antibody recognize?

=== layout: two-panels



# Antibody Recognition


@left


- Antigen exposure prompts production of an antibody.
- The antibody recognizes a specific antigenic determinant (epitope).


