=== layout: one-plus-two-panels


# Gel Filtration


@left


- Gel filtration chromatography allows the separation of proteins on the basis of size.
- A glass column is filled with porous beads.
- When a protein solution is passed over the beads, large proteins cannot enter the beads and exit the column first.
- Small proteins can enter the beads and thus have a longer path and exit the column last.


@top-right


![Instructor figure related to protein purification chromatography](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_037.gif)


@bottom-right


![Instructor figure related to protein purification chromatography](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_038.jpg)

