![Instructor figure related to insect-cell protein expression](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_073.jpg)

=== layout: one-plus-two-panels


# Baculovirus


@left

- Mammalian culture: delicate; costly media
- Insect cells: robust; simpler growth conditions
- Baculovirus vector carries the target gene
- Infection drives high protein expression
- Eukaryotic processing; distinct glycosylation

@top-right


![Instructor figure related to insect-cell protein expression](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_073.jpg)


@bottom-right


![Instructor figure related to insect-cell protein expression](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_071.jpg)

=== layout: two-panels


# Complex Glycosylation


@left


![Instructor figure related to insect-cell protein expression](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_071.jpg)


@right


- Mammals and insects share several steps in the pathway for post-translational glycosylation of asparagine residues in proteins.
- However, the final modifications differ as shown.
- In particular, mammals add sialic acid residues to the ends of the glycosyl chains, whereas insects do not.

=== layout: two-panels


# Baculovirus Expression Vector


@left


![Instructor figure related to insect-cell protein expression](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_072.jpg)


@right

- Transfer vector: target gene + polyhedrin promoter/terminator
- Vector assembled in E. coli
- Co-transfect insect cells with vector + viral genome
- Homologous recombination inserts the target cassette
- Select recombinant virus
- Infect culture; express protein

=== layout: two-panels


# Bacmid Shuttle Vector


@left


- Bacmids are primarily baculovirus genomes with the addition of a bacterial origin of replication, a multiple cloning site, and an antibiotic resistance gene.
  - These sequences allow the bacmid to survive in E. coli but still infect insect cells.


@right


![Instructor figure related to insect-cell protein expression](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_073.jpg)

=== layout: one-plus-two-panels


